Email phishing : attackers send fake emails pretending to be trusted organisation such as banks to trick the users into vlicking malicious links or sharing personal personal information.
Spear phishing : a targeted phishing attack aimed at a specific individual or organisation. Attackers use personal information to make their messages appear genuine.
Smishing : Attackers send fradulent text messages pretending to be legitimate companies to trick people into clicking harmful links or providing personal details.
Vishing : criminals use phone calls to impersonate trusted individuals or organisations and persuade victims to reveal confidential information.
